sed":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 1.79"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":0,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":46.68,"default_fair_val":46.68,"premium_pct":-69.8,"is_undervalued":true,"pe_trailing":7.9,"pe_forward":7,"pb_trailing":0.9,"pb_forward":0.8,"div_yield":0.02,"ps_ratio":1.6,"fcf_to_ev":11.34,"fcf_to_mcap":16.03,"liab_to_assets":53.3,"cash_to_assets":13.6,"current_ratio":1.79,"roe":11.5,"roa":5.2,"moat":{"ticker":"SSL","period":"2026Q4","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Sasol 的品牌在化工產業中並無顯著的定價權。其產品多為大宗商品或中間體，價格主要受市場供需影響，而非品牌溢價。與競爭對手相比，Sasol 的品牌識別度不高，難以支撐顯著的價格差異。其商業模式依賴於規模化生產和成本控制，而非獨特的品牌價值，這使其在面對價格波動時較為脆弱。","comment_en":"Sasol's brand does not possess significant pricing power within the chemical industry. Its products are largely commodities or intermediates, with prices primarily dictated by market supply and demand rather than brand premiums. Compared to competitors, Sasol's brand recognition is low, making it difficult to support substantial price differentiation. Its business model relies on large-scale production and cost control, not unique brand value, rendering it vulnerable to price fluctuations."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Sasol 在特定技術領域，如煤轉化技術（CTL）和氣轉化技術（GTL），擁有專利和技術訣竅。然而，這些技術的壁壘相對有限，且面臨來自其他替代技術和生產方法的競爭。監管環境對化工產業影響深遠，但 Sasol 並未展現出能將監管優勢轉化為持久護城河的能力。其專利組合不足以構成強大的進入壁壘。","comment_en":"Sasol holds patents and technical know-how in specific areas, such as coal-to-liquids (CTL) and gas-to-liquids (GTL) technologies. However, the barriers associated with these technologies are relatively limited and face competition from other alternative technologies and production methods. The regulatory environment significantly impacts the chemical industry, but Sasol has not demonstrated an ability to translate regulatory advantages into a durable moat. Its patent portfolio is insufficient to form a strong entry barrier."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"Sasol 的客戶在轉換供應商時會面臨一定的成本，尤其是在需要特定規格或與其生產流程緊密整合的產品時。然而，這些轉換成本並非高到足以形成強大的客戶黏性。許多大宗化學品市場的客戶仍有較大的選擇空間，並且會尋求更具成本效益的替代品。因此，轉換成本提供的護城河相對較弱。","comment_en":"Sasol's customers face certain costs when switching suppliers, particularly for products requiring specific specifications or tight integration with their production processes. However, these switching costs are not high enough to create strong customer stickiness. Customers in many commodity chemical markets have considerable choice and will seek more cost-effective alternatives. Therefore, the moat provided by switching costs is relatively weak."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":1,"comment_zh":"Sasol 的業務模式不涉及網絡效應。其產品的價值和銷售不依賴於用戶數量的增加而提升。在化工產業中，網絡效應通常出現在平台型業務或社交媒體等領域，這與 Sasol 的大宗商品和中間體業務性質截然不同。因此，此維度幾乎沒有護城河可言。","comment_en":"Sasol's business model does not involve network effects. The value and sales of its products do not increase with the growing number of users. In the chemical industry, network effects are typically found in platform businesses or social media, which is fundamentally different from Sasol's commodity and intermediate business. Consequently, there is virtually no moat in this dimension."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Sasol 在煤轉化和氣轉化技術方面擁有顯著的規模優勢，尤其是在其南非的基地。大規模的生產設施使其能夠實現較低的單位生產成本，這在成本敏感的大宗商品市場中是一個重要的競爭優勢。然而，其依賴特定資源（如煤炭）的模式也帶來了風險，且全球能源轉型可能影響其長期成本結構的穩固性。","comment_en":"Sasol possesses a significant scale advantage in its coal-to-liquids and gas-to-liquids technologies, particularly at its South African base. Large-scale production facilities enable it to achieve lower unit production costs, which is a crucial competitive advantage in cost-sensitive commodity markets. However, its reliance on specific resources (like coal) also introduces risks, and the global energy transition may affect the stability of its long-term cost structure."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Sasol 在南非擁有獨特的煤炭資源和相關的生產設施，這構成了其業務的地理資產壁壘。這些資產的開發和運營需要巨大的資本投入和專業知識，使得新進入者難以複製。然而，這種地理集中性也帶來了政治和監管風險，並且其對特定資源的依賴性限制了其在全球範圍內的廣泛應用。","comment_en":"Sasol's ownership of unique coal resources and related production facilities in South Africa constitutes a geographical asset barrier for its business. The development and operation of these assets require substantial capital investment and expertise, making them difficult for new entrants to replicate. However, this geographical concentration also brings political and regulatory risks, and its dependence on specific resources limits its widespread application globally."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Sasol 在其核心的煤轉化和氣轉化技術方面展現了一定的運營效率，能夠將低成本的原料轉化為高價值的產品。然而，其歷史上的項目執行問題和財務表現波動表明，運營效率並非其最穩固的護城河。公司近年來面臨較大的債務壓力，這可能影響其持續優化運營效率的能力。","comment_en":"Sasol demonstrates a degree of operational efficiency in its core coal-to-liquids and gas-to-liquids technologies, enabling it to convert low-cost feedstock into higher-value products. However, its historical project execution issues and fluctuating financial performance indicate that operational efficiency is not its strongest moat. The company has faced significant debt pressure in recent years, which may impact its ability to continuously optimize operational efficiency."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Sasol 的資本配置歷史記錄並不理想，尤其是在大型項目（如美國路易斯安那州的 GTL 工廠）上出現了重大的超支和延誤，導致嚴重的財務損失。這表明管理層在資本配置決策上存在較大挑戰。儘管公司近年來致力於削減債務和優化資產負債表，但其過往的記錄削弱了市場對其未來資本配置能力的信心。","comment_en":"Sasol's track record in capital allocation is not ideal, particularly with significant cost overruns and delays in major projects (such as the GTL plant in Louisiana, USA), leading to substantial financial losses. This indicates considerable challenges in management's capital allocation decisions. Although the company has focused on debt reduction and balance sheet optimization in recent years, its past performance has weakened market confidence in its future capital allocation capabilities."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":4,"comment_zh":"Sasol 的客戶保留率受到其產品性質和市場競爭的影響。雖然部分客戶因技術整合或特定需求而具有一定的黏性，但 Sasol 的產品多為大宗商品，客戶在尋求更優價格或替代方案時，轉換的可能性仍然存在。公司需要持續提供有競爭力的價格和穩定的供應來維持客戶關係，這表明其客戶保留並非基於難以撼動的壁壘。","comment_en":"Sasol's customer retention rate is influenced by the nature of its products and market competition. While some customers exhibit a degree of stickiness due to technical integration or specific needs, many of Sasol's products are commodities, and the possibility of customers switching when seeking better prices or alternatives remains. The company needs to continuously offer competitive pricing and stable supply to maintain customer relationships, indicating that its customer retention is not based on insurmountable barriers."},"m10_durability":{"score":3,"comment_zh":"Sasol 的業務模式，特別是其對化石燃料的依賴，面臨著長期可持續性的挑戰。全球能源轉型和對環境保護的日益重視，可能對其核心業務構成威脅。雖然公司正在探索轉型之路，但其現有資產和技術的長期價值存在不確定性。其護城河的持久性受到宏觀經濟和環境政策變化的顯著影響。","comment_en":"Sasol's business model, particularly its reliance on fossil fuels, faces long-term sustainability challenges. The global energy transition and increasing emphasis on environmental protection may pose threats to its core business. Although the company is exploring a path of transformation, the long-term value of its existing assets and technologies is uncertain. The durability of its moat is significantly affected by macroeconomic and environmental policy changes."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Sasol Limited 的經濟護城河整體偏弱，其核心競爭力主要體現在規模化生產和特定地理資源的利用上（M5, M6）。然而，公司缺乏強大的品牌定價權（M1）、網絡效應（M4）和顯著的客戶轉換成本（M3）。過往的資本配置失誤（M8）和對化石燃料的依賴性（M10）也削弱了其護城河的持久性。雖然在某些技術領域有專利（M2）和一定的運營效率（M7），但這些並不足以構成堅固的長期壁壘。其商業模式更接近於商品型，易受市場波動和行業轉型影響。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Sasol Limited's economic moat is generally weak, with its core competitiveness primarily reflected in large-scale production and the utilization of specific geographical resources (M5, M6). However, the company lacks strong brand pricing power (M1), network effects (M4), and significant customer switching costs (M3). Past capital allocation missteps (M8) and its reliance on fossil fuels (M10) also undermine the durability of its moat. While it holds patents in certain technological areas (M2) and exhibits some operational efficiency (M7), these are insufficient to form a robust long-term barrier. Its business model is more akin to a commodity type, susceptible to market volatility and industry transitions.","evidenceHash":"5987b46b712e5a41263e4ac1f2203d05e70db2f578a08f7339995c690025b2b2","assessmentPolicy":"buffett-moat-v3","model":"gemini-2.5-flash-lite","provider":"Vertex AI"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":"staleEvidence","evidenceHash":"5987b46b712e5a41263e4ac1f2203d05e70db2f578a08f7339995c690025b2b2","currentEvidenceHash":"177f5a120707fe8f0976dc20d3852d8153cb929374eb628703ed78f73854aa98"},"fScore":{"score":7,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-06-30","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"grey","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"ZAR","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-12T08:14:39.207Z","evidenceHash":"c1ce8ce0ee1480c0c42074d1c853790e199295ca194fff4e7cde1a4069e09708","mcapFx":{"asOf":"2026-11-11","from":"USD","to":"ZAR","fromUsdPerUnit":1,"toUsdPerUnit":0.060492408202770555,"fromObservationDate":"2026-11-11","toObservationDate":"2026-11-06"}},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2026-06-30","period":"FY 2026","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"ZAR","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-11-12T08:14:39.207Z","evidenceHash":"c1ce8ce0ee1480c0c42074d1c853790e199295ca194fff4e7cde1a4069e09708"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SSL.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/SSL.png","website":"https://www.sasol.com","ceo":"Simon Baloyi","full_time_employees":"27107","description":"Based in Johannesburg, South Africa, Sasol Limited functions as an integrated chemical and energy enterprise with a global footprint, organized into six primary segments: Mining, Gas, Fuels, and its Chemicals operations spanning Africa, America, and Eurasia. The company delivers a diverse range of chemical products, encompassing various monomers, ammonia, carbon compounds, chlor alkali, explosives, fertilizers, glycols, polymers, and waxes, in addition to specialty chemicals like lacquer thinners and phenolics. Its offerings also include industrial and household cleaning agents, degreasers, and a comprehensive suite of fuels such as bitumen, motor fuels, gas-to-liquid fuels, and other refined petroleum products like illuminating paraffin and synthetic kerosene. Beyond manufacturing, Sasol wholesales diesel and petrol, operates coal mines, provides engineering expertise, and actively invests in developing lower-carbon energy solutions. The company is also involved in the exploration, development, production, and distribution of natural gas through pipeline networks. Serving an extensive array of sectors, from automotive, agriculture, and aviation to healthcare, packaging, and textiles, Sasol was founded in 1950 and is headquartered in Johannesburg.","description_en":"Based in Johannesburg, South Africa, Sasol Limited functions as an integrated chemical and energy enterprise with a global footprint, organized into six primary segments: Mining, Gas, Fuels, and its Chemicals operations spanning Africa, America, and Eurasia. The company delivers a diverse range of chemical products, encompassing various monomers, ammonia, carbon compounds, chlor alkali, explosives, fertilizers, glycols, polymers, and waxes, in addition to specialty chemicals like lacquer thinners and phenolics. Its offerings also include industrial and household cleaning agents, degreasers, and a comprehensive suite of fuels such as bitumen, motor fuels, gas-to-liquid fuels, and other refined petroleum products like illuminating paraffin and synthetic kerosene. Beyond manufacturing, Sasol wholesales diesel and petrol, operates coal mines, provides engineering expertise, and actively invests in developing lower-carbon energy solutions. The company is also involved in the exploration, development, production, and distribution of natural gas through pipeline networks. Serving an extensive array of sectors, from automotive, agriculture, and aviation to healthcare, packaging, and textiles, Sasol was founded in 1950 and is headquartered in Johannesburg.","description_zh":"Sasol Limited（美股代碼：SSL）為 Basic Materials 領域之重要企業，專注於 Chemicals 業務，具備清晰之商業壁壘與現金流創造能力。","address":"Sasol Place","city":"Sandton","state":"GT","zip":"2196","country":"ZA","phone":"27 10 344 5000","full_address":"Sasol Place, Sandton, GT 2196, ZA","range_52w":"5.97-18.19","year_high":18.19,"year_low":5.97,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":5.97,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Kahla Vuyo Dominic","title":"director, officer: EVP, Commercial and Legal","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":21640,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Kahla Vuyo Dominic","title":"director, officer: EVP, Commercial and Legal","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":21640,"price":14.14,"total_val":0.31},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Herrmann Christiaan Horst","title":"officer: EVP, Marketing and Sales","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":3434,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Herrmann Christiaan Horst","title":"officer: EVP, Marketing and Sales","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":3300,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Bruns Walt Paul","title":"director, officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"A-Award","shares":1989,"price":0,"total_val":0},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Bruns Walt Paul","title":"director, officer: Chief Financial Officer","is_buy":false,"action":"S-Sale","shares":1798,"price":14.14,"total_val":0.03},{"date":"2026-10-01","name":"Baloyi Si